# secret-patterns — lista unica de patrones de secreto de alta confianza.
# La leen write-guard.py (Write/Edit/MultiEdit/NotebookEdit) y bash-write-guard.sh (Bash).
# Formato: etiqueta<TAB>accion<TAB>ERE. accion = block (deniega) | advise (solo avisa; el guard de
# Bash la ignora). Subconjunto ERE a proposito: lo que Python re y grep -E leen igual (sin (?i), sin
# lookahead, sin \d ni \-; el guion va al final del corchete). test_guards.sh prueba la paridad.
# Lo que no cabe en ERE (Twilio, asignacion generica con lookahead) vive en write-guard.py.
Anthropic API key	block	sk-ant-[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{20,}
OpenAI API key	block	sk-[a-zA-Z0-9]{20,}
OpenAI project/service-account key	block	sk-(proj|svcacct)-[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{20,}
Stripe live secret key	block	sk_live_[a-zA-Z0-9]{24}
Stripe test secret key	block	sk_test_[a-zA-Z0-9]{24}
AWS Access Key ID	block	AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}
Google API key	block	AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}
GitHub Personal Access Token	block	ghp_[a-zA-Z0-9]{36}
GitHub OAuth token	block	gho_[a-zA-Z0-9]{36}
GitHub server-to-server token	block	ghs_[a-zA-Z0-9]{36}
GitHub user-to-server token	block	ghu_[a-zA-Z0-9]{36}
GitHub fine-grained PAT	block	github_pat_[a-zA-Z0-9_]{82}
Slack bot token	block	xoxb-[0-9]+-[0-9A-Za-z-]+
Slack user token	block	xoxp-[0-9]+-[0-9A-Za-z-]+
PEM private key	block	-----BEGIN (RSA |EC |OPENSSH |DSA |ENCRYPTED )?PRIVATE KEY-----
npm access token	block	npm_[a-zA-Z0-9]{36}
SendGrid API key	block	SG\.[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{22}\.[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{43}
Databricks API token	block	dapi[a-z0-9]{32}
Azure storage connection string	block	DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=
JWT token (hardcoded)	advise	eyJ[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{10,}\.eyJ[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{10,}\.[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{10,}
